 "provenance_note": "Registry-native cohort: 206 AACT trials posted both sensitivity and specificity as percentages; 66 had a usable modality + subgroup denominators to reconstruct a 2x2 (TP=round(Se%xn1), TN=round(Sp%xn0); fail-closed on implausible rate / tiny subgroup). The per-study summary is the DIAGNOSTIC ODDS RATIO (DOR=TP*TN/(FP*FN)), carried in the ratio slots and labelled 'diagnostic OR' - it is NOT a time-to-event hazard ratio. AACT-reconstructed 2x2, NOT 2x2 tables read from full text and NOT a dual-screened systematic review. Synthesis hierarchy: Bayesian bivariate (Reitsma) league (dta_league.json) ranked by Youden J; the engine flags the cross-modality ranking as cross-target heterogeneity (mixed cancer sites) -> not a clean winner."
}